            <ArticleTitle>Images in cardiovascular medicine: ruptured aneurysm of the sinus of Valsava.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>184-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 27 year old woman presented with a two year history of cardiac symptoms. Echocardiographic examination revealed a ruptured aneurysm of the sinus of Valsava. Of note the patient was known to be HIV positive.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
